1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,840
We've been working with the power and communications companies, and they've got cell phone service and web access restored in certain areas.

2
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:11,600
And how long do we think it will take for the whole prefecture?

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:17,500
There's still no way for us to tell. With transportation being so limited at this juncture, repairs are slow going.

4
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:19,680
Do we have an idea of the damage yet?

5
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:27,840
Seems we've still only heard from a few areas, but those that can are beginning to report their casualties and evacuation status, as well as the damages to homes and infrastructure.

6
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:30,100
We need to obtain those numbers quickly.

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:36,360
There's been flooding throughout the entire prefecture, but it appears as though the north and the Sajiro and Sanshin areas were hit the hardest of all.

8
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,980
The water is gradually beginning to recede, but it's far too early to know much.

9
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:43,360
The initial damage could still prove quite risky.

10
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:48,220
Right. I'll be sure to stay in touch with fire services, the JSDF, and the Social Welfare Council, sir.

11
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,600
Thank you. Please do that.

12
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:51,640
Governor!

13
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:52,020
You're still!

14
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:55,900
I need to speak with you! You should put a rush on repairs in the Tosu area!

15
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,060
Please, sir! Tosu is a critical intersection in Kyushu!

16
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:00,640
We should move you out of this room.

17
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:03,980
If we get transportation running, that means everything else will go faster, too!

18
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:08,480
We're fully aware of that fact, sir. We need civilians to be patient for now.

19
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,920
But Saga's future is depending on this!

20
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,580
Get him out of here.

21
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,620
You have to let Franshoushu perform!

22
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:17,060
Governor?

23
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,080
Please believe me! This concert will help Saga!

24
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:24,400
Because if Franshoushu gets to sing, then Saga will be revived!

25
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,540
But the people need a way to get over there!

26
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:29,220
That's why I'm begging you to fix the Tosu area!

27
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:30,940
Please, you have to!

28
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,840
Look, sir, I think we've heard—

29
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:34,580
I'm not talking to you!

30
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:44,140
What these residents need right now is to know that everything's going to work out okay.

31
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:48,300
Just one thing to unify us so we can face this tragedy together.

32
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,340
And Franshoushu can give them that.

33
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:54,120
So please, make the call, sir.

34
00:01:54,120 --> 00:02:03,320
Dude, what were you thinking?

35
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:09,500
Tatsumi here.

36
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:10,660
It's Okuba.

37
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:12,420
I finally got through.

38
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:13,620
Any luck yet?

39
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:16,280
You're demanding results right from the get-go?

40
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:20,120
You've got no idea the hoops I had to jump through to score a chopper right up here.

41
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:24,720
This is tricky.

42
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:28,080
Yeah, a charity concert sounds real nice in theory.

43
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:32,700
But then, who's going to jump on board with an event that might not happen?

44
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,100
There's just no guarantee.

45
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,060
You've got what it takes.

46
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,500
Don't be so sure.

47
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:40,160
It's been a full decade since I ran with this crowd.

48
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,380
I believe in you.

49
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:46,960
Just so you understand, it's way too early for me to say the same thing about you.

50
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:49,220
But—but I figure—

51
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:55,440
I'll do my best.

52
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:58,020
And let the gods sort out the rest of it.

53
00:02:58,380 --> 00:03:00,340
I'm not leaving a damn thing up to a god.

54
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,460
Not after everything that's happened.

55
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:05,560
Hmm.

56
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:08,920
I guess he's got a point.

57
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:23,820
There's only a week to go until the concert.

58
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:24,880
I know.

59
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:26,860
I'm getting some butterflies, aren't you?

60
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:28,580
This is a good kind of tension, though.

61
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:31,860
I mean, we've been totally in the zone over the last few days.

62
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:34,020
I don't think we've ever been this focused.

63
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:35,020
Hey, you're right.

64
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,180
I noticed the same thing.

65
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:37,060
Yeah, me too.

66
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:38,100
I wonder why.

67
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,920
Guess what my Tamagotchi did.

68
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:44,080
Oya-ji-chi and me-me-ji-chi got together and they mixed into a me-me-oya-ji-chi.

69
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,560
What's that got to do with this?

70
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,980
I'm just saying, we've all been on a roll lately.

71
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:54,760
It's strange.

72
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:58,300
I can't help but wonder if he's watching over us from the heavens even now.

73
00:03:58,420 --> 00:03:59,280
Who do you mean?

74
00:03:59,520 --> 00:03:59,800
Hmm.

75
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:03,780
Oh, someone who was precious to me when I was alive.

76
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:10,420
I bet he's up there cheering us on, just like Mommy is.

77
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:11,920
Nice.

78
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:13,800
Yes.

79
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:18,880
We've worked hard to make it this far, and now we just have to give them a great performance

80
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,840
on the day of the show.

81
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:22,080
I hope a lot of people will be able to make it there.

82
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:22,740
Damn it.

83
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:27,060
If it weren't for that stupid storm screwing up everything, we would be passing out flyers

84
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,320
and building up a buzz on the radio right about now.

85
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,760
Uh, hang on.

86
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,800
What day is it today?

87
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:35,380
Like the day of the week?

88
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:39,280
Come to think of it, we have been paying a lot more attention to the dates than what day

89
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:39,860
it is lately.

90
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,320
Hey, I'm not sure, but I think it's Friday?

91
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:43,040
Huh?

92
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:44,840
But that's the day we go on our show!

93
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,240
Crap, this sucks!

94
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,480
I gotta get ready fast!

95
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:50,240
Um, but with everything that's going on...

96
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,960
I know things are bad, but I want to.

97
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,540
And besides, we already missed out on one show.

98
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,140
Nobody's going to blame you.

99
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:57,840
All of Saga's in crisis.

100
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,720
Are you really going to go?

101
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:01,100
Damn right I am!

102
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:04,520
Because if we don't do everything we can, then Saga's going to lose itself!

103
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,120
Um, you're here on the wrong day.

104
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:09,600
Today's actually Sunday.

105
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:11,740
Oh, we're sorry, sir.

106
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,520
I'm going to kill you!

107
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:14,620
You're double dead!

108
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,460
The whole group?

109
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:16,940
How'd you all get mixed up?

110
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,520
You know what?

111
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:19,460
I have a great idea.

112
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:21,880
Since you're here, why don't you go on the air now?

113
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:23,940
Is that okay?

114
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:24,680
Of course!

115
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:28,460
We're all set to broadcast, but none of our regular personalities are able to get over

116
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,260
here at the moment with the way the roads have been.

117
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,380
It's only fair to tell you, though.

118
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:34,660
There's no way to know how many people are going to tune in.

119
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:36,180
Oh, that's totally fine.

120
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,600
Thank you very much, sir.

121
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:38,600
All right!

122
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:39,320
Let's go!

123
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:42,920
We'll continue to bring you updates regarding the affected areas.

124
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:46,940
Please feel free to contact us with any relevant information as well.

125
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:51,800
Now, for today's show, we have some wonderful guests with us in the studio.

126
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:53,220
Good evening!

127
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:54,400
We're Frond Shoo Shoo!

128
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,220
Ka-chee!

129
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:57,360
What's wrong, my mom?

130
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,740
Your Frond Shoo Shoo sense is tingling, huh?

131
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:02,220
Well, she is a superfan and a former member.

132
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,900
So, uh, listen, Saga.

133
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,840
With a whole disaster, it's pretty freaking rough out there for everybody right now.

134
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:17,040
And, uh, I don't know where you're hearing this from or if you're okay, but I'm sure

135
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:20,140
you're probably scared and maybe kind of lonely, too.

136
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:24,760
Hell, you might just be super pissed off about everything that's happened here in Saga

137
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:27,100
lately, but...

138
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:29,080
How do I say this?

139
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:34,280
I just want you to know that right now, people are doing what they can to help in all kinds

140
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,080
of different ways.

141
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,540
We learned that at the shelter we stayed in.

142
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:42,900
When stuff like this happens, it shows you what people can do if they work together.

143
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:49,900
I don't know if I'm making any sense, but I think that's an important thing to remember.

144
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:53,980
That's why Frond Shoo Shoo's been thinking about what we can do.

145
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:55,880
You know, to help Saga.

146
00:06:56,880 --> 00:07:04,480
So we talked it over, and to connect to all of you, we figured that the best way is through

147
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,080
our music.

148
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:11,140
We want to bring some cheer, which is why we'll be doing a live concert soon.

149
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:15,480
It'll be March 8th at the Ekimai Fudo-san Stadium.

150
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:21,740
You may have heard that we performed a show at that same spot, and we stunk out loud.

151
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:26,640
The crowd was tiny, we freaked out, everything about it sucked.

152
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:29,740
And just like last time...

153
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:31,920
Actually, scratch that.

154
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,380
This time, it could be even worse.

155
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:39,600
But still, we're going to give you guys the greatest performance ever.

156
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:43,800
And after that big storm, I'm sure some people will say that we shouldn't do this.

157
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:47,800
But music can help, and our singing is all we have to offer you.

158
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:52,380
I don't know if we'll really be able to make people feel better, but...

159
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:56,520
We're going to be up there on that stage, trying our best to make you smile.

160
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,040
Even just a little bit.

161
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:01,320
After all, we're Franshu-shu.

162
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,460
That's what we do!

163
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:16,720
Everybody got your stuff?

164
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:17,480
Ready!

165
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:20,760
We don't know what it's like out here, so let's be careful.

166
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:23,800
Eh, I'm sure we'll make it all right.

167
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,600
We're zombies, so what's there for us to be afraid of?

168
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,580
Okay, let's get going then.

169
00:08:32,460 --> 00:09:02,440
We'll be right back.

170
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:32,440
We'll be right back.

171
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:37,180
Anyway, the show's in 16 days.

172
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:39,400
Call time is 10 a.m. sharp.

173
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:44,020
That idiot, Shades.

174
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:46,440
He must have got the date screwed up somehow.

175
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,560
Though, we were confused too for a while there.

176
00:09:49,560 --> 00:10:02,460
I'm not going to give up.

177
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:06,780
I don't care how awful it gets.

178
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:15,500
Even if we try our hardest and it still goes badly, I'll keep on singing.

179
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,260
No god will stop us.

180
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:19,920
No devil will either.

181
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:23,740
We'll outlast everything and everybody that dares to stand in our way,

182
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,540
because we're getting our revenge!

183
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:34,460
Those two really are ride or die, huh?

184
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:47,500
Those two really are ride or die, huh?

185
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:48,180
That's true.

186
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:50,620
They've been with us for every step of the journey.

187
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:51,620
They've been with us for every step of the journey.

