They've been with us for every step of the journey.

189
00:10:55,620 --> 00:11:25,600
They've been with us for every step of the journey.

190
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,020
We're above Saga's Ekimai Fudo-san Stadium,

191
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,400
where the damage from the recent flooding is still visible.

192
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:34,440
The charity concert being held here by local idol group Franshushu

193
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:36,140
is drawing a sizable crowd.

194
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:40,980
NBK Fukuoka caught up with these homegrown celebrities at a shelter last week,

195
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:44,560
and the response from our viewers was overwhelming to say the least.

196
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:49,060
Not only that, nationwide newspapers have been advertising the event,

197
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:51,600
which has also increased visibility significantly.

198
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:55,300
The concert's abuzz in social media circles as well.

199
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:59,280
Two of the most trending posts were from Shiori Baba of Iron Frill,

200
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:01,180
one of Japan's largest idol groups,

201
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,640
and famous child actor Light Ozara.

202
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:07,380
It looks like the arena isn't quite set up for the big concert yet,

203
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:10,680
but you can see the massive crowd that's already assembled here

204
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,300
to show their support for Saga.

205
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:16,280
Thanks to favorable stories in five big papers,

206
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:18,820
the event gained sponsors from all over Japan,

207
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:21,720
starting with Saga's own Hisanaka Pharmaceuticals.

208
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:23,640
And it's not just Japan, either.

209
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:27,300
As the news continues to spread worldwide about the disaster in Kyushu,

210
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:31,380
people in various countries all across the world have begun offering assistance.

211
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:32,780
Like I told you,

212
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,520
the answer can always be found in Saga.

213
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:39,360
We're seeing something that only happens once in a lifetime.

214
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:42,120
the entire world is coming together for Saga.

215
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,560
No, for Japan!

216
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:45,980
It's a decisive moment in history.

217
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,600
The climax of an epic Saga!

218
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,240
I cannot thank you enough.

219
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:56,520
Yeah, just so you understand,

220
